WEBVTT

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.540
He's got good moves. He's well-trained.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.130
Call us over at any time.
I'd love to help the team out.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.510
There you go.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.010
Just changing up your jabs
can change up the whole flow.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.350
You need to always be
thinking as you move.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.770
Your opponent's not just gonna
sit there and take the punches.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.640
What's important is to maintain
a balance with your Gear

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.940
and still be able to move fast.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.270
Slowpoke boxers aren't
gonna bring in a crowd.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.070
Matches only mean anything
if they can fill those seats.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.120
Sounds like things are going well.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.370
They're the perfect duo.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.200
Even better than us?

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.620
{=0}Team Nowhere

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.550
I got a big one!

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.010
So did we!

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.350
Hey, it's Abuhachi!

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.680
Hey.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.560
Oicho, let's go.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.860
Team Nowhere

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.660
All right, you guys better behave.
Even if it's just for now.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:40.290
Because I'm awesome, I managed to secure
the whole sports column for you guys.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.960
Hey, Bonjiri. We can't see the veggies.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.540
Come on, Joe and Aragaki.
Smiling's not gonna kill you.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.090
All right, here we go!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.930
Team Nowhere

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.850
Say cheese!

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:06.810
Team Nowhere

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.990
"MEGALOBOX 2"

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.160
Abuhachi's Shop

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.970
Probably a bit too late to worry
about what happened now.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.970
I just need to tell me what happened.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.680
I won't cause you any trouble.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.640
Trouble?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.520
You seem to have the wrong
idea about something.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.530
I don't give a shit about
your circumstances,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.570
nor do I want to know.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.410
Sorry to bother you.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.500
Everything got washed away. All of it.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.130
A typhoon flooded the river.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.050
The only silver lining was
no one was injured or killed.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.380
Boss!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.470
I'm done with the maintenance,

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.510
so I'm gonna take this over to the
Department of Veterans Affairs.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.810
I'll go follow up on the
guys who still need

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.350
to pay their tabs then
I'm gonna head home.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.150
Didn't you say you
wouldn't take apprentices?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.490
You've really got some nerve.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.240
It's been five years since you
abandoned those kids.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.120
Oicho, I'm sorry...

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.250
How are the others...? The other kids?

00:03:52.290 --> 00:04:00.260
"Abuhachi's Shop"

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.220
We're all fine, no thanks to you.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.180
What about Sachio?

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.720
How's he doing?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.600
Do you really think he wants to see you?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.610
It's all in the past now.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.240
Nowhere

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.710
It's all in the past now.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.970
So even if he had another surgery...

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.930
Yes. It's already spread
to this lymph nodes,

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.810
so it's highly doubtful we'd
be able to remove it all.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.350
I'd like to talk about where we
can go from here for his treatment.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.400
Does he have any family?

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.940
We're his family.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.440
Hang in there

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.110
We planted some grapes yesterday!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.740
We did everything we could,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:48.660
but I'm afraid Mr. Nanbu's only got
about six months left at most.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.950
The leaves are super jagged and cool!

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:48.660
We're all waiting for you to
come home all better, Pops.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.120
If he's able to undergo the latest
but expensive procedures,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.960
he may live a bit longer.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:02.260
But his wish was to spend the rest of
his days peacefully with his family.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:12.270
I heard on the news that Yuri's precious
student wanted a match with you.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.560
What was his name again--

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.980
You mean Liu?

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.440
Yeah, that's the guy.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.690
Joe, you got the offer, didn't ya?

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.990
It's an exhibition match to try to get

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.830
Joe back in the ring after he's
been away for more than a year.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:37.000
Even if it's not an official match,
if the kid's serious, why not accept?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.050
Think of it as a gift to Yuri,
who returned to the world of Megalobox.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:48.260
I actually got to fight him in the ring.
I've got no regrets.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.310
We sure had fun...
Though that's in the past now.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:14.040
Joe, Sachio. We gave it a good fight.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:19.920
I don't plan on wasting the rest of my
life just to gain a little borrowed time.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.510
Are you sure?

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:31.100
I don't need to tell you what's
most important, now do I?

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.140
Right...

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.070
Gym Nowhere

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.540
I'm home.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.460
Welcome home.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.920
Pops was doing well today.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.880
Looks like he's getting
his appetite back a little.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.090
Sachio.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.510
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.940
Pops said the same thing.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.150
That they're taking care
of him at the hospital,

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.190
so I don't have to come by every day.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.030
So I gave him a piece of my mind.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:37.280
"Congratulations on your
victory at Megalonia!!"

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:28.240
"I came here because I wanted to.
You can't tell me what to do."

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.830
And then he said, "I want some
peace and quiet, so scram."

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:37.200
But when I was about to leave,
he looked so lonely.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.250
Well, at least that side
of him is being honest.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:46.510
"Figure out what you want to do yourself."

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.300
Talk about a contradiction.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.640
Is there really nothing else we can do?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.180
Sachio.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:04.110
I wanted to honor Pops' wishes but...
is this really the right answer?

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.980
I just don't know anymore.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.700
Say, Joe...

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.370
Is this really the end?!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:38.550
{=1}Team Nowhere

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.430
"Congratulations on your
victory at Megalonia!!"

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.730
I don't want you to suffer.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.360
But I don't want to
give up without trying.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.200
Please, Pops...

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.620
I need you to fight with me one more time.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.960
So you can't even let me die in peace.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.420
Fine.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.010
My luck ran out the moment
I met you anyway.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.330
Who's there?

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.220
You're...

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.770
This is our house.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.900
Get the hell out!

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:22.640
I'm sorry... Sachio.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.820
Sachio...

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:57.010
I heard you were back, so I came
to beat the shit outta you,

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.130
but apparently someone beat me to it.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.720
Aragaki...

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:14.690
It was just about a year ago.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.360
Sachio realized the river was flooding,

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:21.160
so he gathered all the other kids
into the truck and they got to safety.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.870
They might've not made
if he realized it any later.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.370
Apparently, they didn't get any
evacuation warnings over there.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:35.460
I was shocked when they showed up in the
middle of the night soaked to the bone.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:43.340
An orphanage run by Shirato
took in the smaller kids.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:48.180
Sachio figured they'd be safe there,
so he asked if they could stay there.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:52.310
The other four lived
here for a while but...

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.810
...they're not kids anymore.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:58.650
As you saw, Oicho became
Mr. Abuhachi's apprentice.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:11.240
"Gym
Nowhere
Opening
Commemoration"

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:03.240
Santa's a freelance reporter
writing about Megalo-boxing.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.240
Bonjiri became a chef and
opened up his own restaurant.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.160
It's just a tiny place located
on the outskirts of town,

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.160
but he's actually got his own place.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.290
And Sachio...

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.210
Where is he right now?

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:25.590
He asked me to teach him
Megalo-boxing, so I did.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.060
I knew instantly he wasn't
mean to be a boxer,

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:32.810
but once I saw the look in his eyes,
I couldn't stop him.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:43.780
After about six months passed, he said
he found a place to stay, and left.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:49.330
I found out that he was doing underground
boxing matches soon after.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.120
You're up, kid.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:15:00.590
I honestly don't care why
you decided to come back.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:06.180
But I can't tell you how many
times I wished you were here.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:10.720
They managed to get
over this on their own.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:15.890
No one needs you anymore,
and there's nowhere for you to go.

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.030
What's the matter, shrimpy?
You ain't swingin'!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.370
What? Ya scared?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.700
The hell kind of punch was that?

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.290
You missed, kid!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.460
Oh, dear. Guess he's just not getting it.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.130
The kid's hopeless.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:06.030
You're not gonna last long
in the ring fighting like that.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:10.910
Get away from me.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.950
I don't know what
possessed you to come back

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.040
but get the hell out of this
town once you're done.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.960
Don't ever show your
face around here again.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:28.680
The guy who kept giving everyone dreams
is the one who should've died.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.100
What do you mean, you accepted the match?!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.350
Don't scowl at me like that.

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.690
"'Gearless' Joe vs the Rookie Liu in an
Exhibition Match! The legendary champ
returns 2 years after Megalonia!!"

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.810
You said you were never

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.610
getting in that ring again!

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.950
This is one last job before I retire.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:53.740
I'm gonna win that prize money and get
Pops the best treatment he can get.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:57.660
Does Pops know about this?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.120
Don't worry about it.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:04.170
You guys went to see him today,
didn't you? How's he holding up?

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.130
He was mostly asleep.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:09.680
We talked to him, but we're
not sure if he heard us or not.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.050
Right?

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.180
Yeah...

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:15.390
His meds are too strong,
so he gets sleepy.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:19.310
Pops didn't know who I was.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:21.400
We just need to hold
out a little bit longer.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.270
I'm gonna figure this out.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.690
But you heard the doctor...

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:30.400
He might live a little longer, but he's
never going to fully recover.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.860
And Pops already--

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.700
We don't know that!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.790
H-Hey, sorry about that.
I didn't mean to yell.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:49.720
But listen. The longer Pops lives,
the more hope we have.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.130
I wanna believe that, too.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.140
But...

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:58.640
We managed to make an
impossible dream come true.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.640
Didn't we, Sachio?

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:01.850
Yeah.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:06.110
I need you kids to believe, too.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:10.820
If I win this match, Pops is gonna
come back healthy and happy.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.280
Really?

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.490
Yeah.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:16.950
You've got this, Joe!

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.540
You can't lose!

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.910
Now, let's eat.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.120
Yeah!

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:35.180
Shit.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.310
Pops!

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:40.140
Doctor! Someone! Please!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.940
Pops! Are you okay?! Pops!

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.560
Mr. Nanbu.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.440
Mr. Nanbu, can you hear me?

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:49.820
We'll get him back into bed
once his breathing stabilizes.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.690
Then we'll need to examine him.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:52.900
Joe!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.300
What're you doin'?

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.970
It's a good luck charm.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.350
If it comes off, I'm just
gonna stick it right back on.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.930
Not bad, kid.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.390
Gym Nowhere

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.780
Come on. Is that all you've got?

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:39.120
Liu's a tough opponent, even before you
were away from the ring for two years.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.410
One more minute!

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.670
Let's go see Pops.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:04.520
I'm only helping you out because
Mr. Nanbu asked me to.

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:07.190
I don't agree with you doing this match.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.730
I already made up my mind.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.750
Why won't you go see Pops?

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.260
You know why. I've got a match coming up.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:42.430
Who the hell cares about the match?

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.970
It's you that Pops needs, Joe!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:48.020
Even if it's just for a little bit.
Stay by his side!

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.350
Joe, please!

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.830
That's enough.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:07.000
I promised Pops that I would fight.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.410
I told you!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:11.460
If we get this prize money,
we might be able to save him.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:14.040
The longer Pops lives,
the more hope we have--

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.550
We don't know that!

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:16.840
What if today's the day?

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:21.550
What if it's tomorrow, huh?
These are all excuses!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:25.760
Quit thinking so much about death.
You're just exhausted.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.770
And you need to quit looking away!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.900
The most important thing right now
is for us to stay by Pops' side.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:34.440
So that he can spend time with his family!

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.230
You're just running away to the ring, Joe!

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:43.240
I just...

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:47.280
"Congratulations on your
victory at Megalonia!!"

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:47.200
We're not a team anymore.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:48.790
We're finished!

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:11.100
It's all in the past now.

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.450
Nowhere
